body:
It seems 

Using the Nightscout Sync (REST-API), I get the devicestatus entries like
```
{
    "_id": {
        "$oid": "5a48a211b137da15c44a78fe"
    },
    "device": "LimiTTer",
    "uploader": {
        "battery": 100
    },
    "created_at": "2017-12-31T08:38:41.007Z"
}
```
and 
```
{
    "_id": {
        "$oid": "5a48a33db137da15c44a78ff"
    },
    "device": "motorola Moto G 2014 LTE",
    "uploader": {
        "battery": 79
    },
    "created_at": "2017-12-31T08:43:41.185Z"
}
```

However, when using the direct MongoDB connection, I get only
```
{
    "_id": {
        "$oid": "5a48ab71abccacee0cf3ced3"
    },
    "uploaderBattery": 86,
    "created_at": "2017-12-31T11:18:41.466+0200"
}
```

It would be nice to get a device string included also when using the direct MongoDB connection.

I ran into the issue when enabling both MongoDB and Nightscout Sync. I want to upload the glucose data to two separate Nightscout instances, as I'm currently testing a loop implementation and have a Nightscout installation for the testing, in addition to the one that's gathering my actual data.
